Scriptname duo_manmadeprobe Hidden
{A PROBE, not a mission. Answers one question before a Delve objective is designed on it: when the game scatters
its man-made decor between POIs (the PCM_CellLoadRequest tree's ManMade branch, manual part 04, 2026-10-20), does
a placed PackIn leave a reference OF THE PACKIN that a script can find?

His idea, 2026-10-20: objectives at the decor pieces ("yeah the objectives at the packins was my thinking. Do we
think we can detect them in the scripts?"). The 121 PIPCMManMade_* PackIns carry no keywords, and only one of
them places an object found nowhere else in the game, so if the PackIn itself is not findable the route is our own
keyworded content in the tree instead.

ONE RUN, THREE COUNTS within the radius of the player:
  1  references of the 121 PIPCMManMade PackIns THEMSELVES   (the question)
  2  references of the 120 objects those PackIns most often place   (the CONTROL: next to a decor piece these
     certainly exist, so a zero here means the search is broken, not that the answer is no)
  3  PrefabPackinPivotDummy alone (placed in 111 of the 121, and in PackIns across the game)
Read it: 1 > 0, the PackIn is the detector. 1 = 0 and 2 > 0, it is not, and the objects are not unique.
Both 0, stand nearer or widen the radius.

NO PLUGIN RECORD. Global functions only, run from the console, nothing in any .esm changes:
    cgf "duo_manmadeprobe.Run" 0        radius 500
    cgf "duo_manmadeprobe.Run" 300      any radius
Stand beside a decor piece out on open ground (like his comms platform screenshot). Once at a POI's centre is a
useful second reading. NUMBERS ONLY in the output (a form cast to a string carries a "<" the box reads as a tag);
the "list index" numbers map to the comment lines below (PackIds and LeafIds, 0-based).
Generated by Eliza from Starfield.esm (scratch probe, 2026-10-20); the lists are data, not hand-edited.}

